# A/B geometry test, reference arm: r2SCAN-3c on the REDUCED system.
#
# 137 atoms: the RC (../rc/displace_minus/job.xyz) with the spectator water
# removed -- water1 = O132 + H131 + H139 (1-based). At the verified TS the
# H-bond chain is
#     O136-H135 ... O134(water2) -> O132(water1) -> O130(ketone O)
#       1.129          1.307           1.897          1.822
# so H135 (the peroxide proton) is delivered to water2 (O134), while water1's
# H131 only H-bonds to the ketone O and -- as the IRC showed -- never moves.
# Water1 is therefore the spectator and is dropped here.
#
# QM region: the previous 20-atom region minus the removed O132/H131/H139,
# remapped to the 137-atom numbering (17 atoms, 0-based).
#
# Pairs with ../../geometry_b973c-xtb/rc/, the B97-3c arm on the identical
# system and QM region, to measure B97-3c's geometry against r2SCAN-3c's and its
# wall time.
! QM/XTB r2SCAN-3c ddCOSMO(Water) opt freq TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
Calc_Hess true
Recalc_Hess 50
END

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
